# XSH posix_spawnattr_getflags() and posix_spawnattr_setflags()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Flags tied to Process Scheduling (POSIX_SPAWN_SETSCHEDPARAM and
# POSIX_SPAWN_SETSCHEDULER) and POSIX_SPAWN_SETSID are used only when the
# header defines them. Effects are shown by really spawning this program as
# a child image. The functions return the error number; errno is not used.

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getflags.001
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getflags.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getflags.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_getflags() on a newly initialised object returns 0 and
           stores 0.
test       t/001-default.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getflags.002
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getflags.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getflags.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       For each flag the header defines, posix_spawnattr_setflags() with that
           flag alone returns 0 and posix_spawnattr_getflags() then
           returns 0 and stores that value.
test       t/002-roundtrip-each.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getflags.003
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getflags.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getflags.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_setflags() with the bitwise OR of POSIX_SPAWN_RESETIDS,
           POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGDEF and POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGMASK returns 0
           and posix_spawnattr_getflags() stores exactly that value.
test       t/003-roundtrip-or.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getflags.004
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getflags.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A later posix_spawnattr_setflags() replaces the earlier value: after
           setting a flag and then 0 the stored value is 0, and after
           setting one flag and then another the stored value is the
           second only.
test       t/004-replaces.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getflags.005
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getflags.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       Two initialised objects keep their own flags: different values set in
           each are read back unchanged from each.
test       t/005-two-objects.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getflags.006
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getflags.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A child spawned with the flag POSIX_SPAWN_SETPGROUP set (spawn-pgroup 0)
           is the leader of a new process group, and after
           posix_spawnattr_setflags() with 0 a child spawned with the
           same object stays in the parent's group.
test       t/006-effect.c
